Zenon error: exhausted search space without finding a proof
@!!BEGIN
@!!type:obligation
@!!id:92
@!!loc:261:13:261:15
@!!status:being proved
@!!prover:zenon
@!!meth:(10 s); time-limit: 10
@!!obl:
ASSUME NEW CONSTANT Values,
       NEW VARIABLE seq,
       NEW VARIABLE sum,
       NEW VARIABLE n,
       NEW VARIABLE pc,
       /\ /\ seq \in Seq(Values)
          /\ sum \in Int
          /\ n \in 1..Len(seq) + 1
          /\ pc \in {"a", "Done"}
       /\ sum = SeqSum([i \in 1..n - 1 |-> seq[i]])
       /\ pc = "Done" => n = Len(seq) + 1 ,
       [Next]_vars ,
       Values \subseteq Int ,
       /\ n' - 1 = n
       /\ Len(s) = n
       /\ s[Len(s)] = seq[n] 
PROVE  SubSeq(s, 1, Len(s) - 1) = [i \in 1..Len(s) - 1 |-> s[i]]

@!!END

